# Notely architecture

Notes app: **Next.js 16** (App Router) + **React 19** + **TypeScript**, **Drizzle/Neon**, **Better Auth**, **TanStack Query**, **Zustand**, **Zod**, **Tailwind/shadcn**.

## Layout

| Area | Path |
|------|------|
| Routes | `src/app/(marketing)`, `(auth)`, `(dashboard)`, `api/**` |
| Auth | `src/lib/auth`, `src/proxy.ts`, `src/lib/api/auth-guard.ts` |
| DB | `src/lib/db` |
| Notes | `src/lib/notes`, `src/app/api/spaces`, `src/app/api/notes`, `src/app/api/tags`, `src/app/api/tasks`, `src/app/api/attachments` |
| UI | `src/components/{ui,notes,landing,layout,forms,auth}` |
| Client state | `src/stores` (Zustand) |
| Env | `src/lib/env.ts` (Zod) |

## Conventions

- Path alias `@/` → `src/`
- Server secrets only through `getEnv()` — never read `process.env` ad hoc in feature code
- API handlers: thin — validate with Zod, auth with `requireSession`, logic in `src/lib/**`
- Prefer existing UI primitives under `src/components/ui` over new one-offs
- App home after login: `/workspace`
- After substantive code edits, run `graphify update .` (see graphify rule)
